            <ArticleTitle>The Case Against Medicaid Expansion in North Carolina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>48-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.18043/ncm.78.1.48</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This commentary argues against Medicaid expansion in North Carolina for 5 reasons: Expansion will reduce access to care for highly vulnerable individuals who are already enrolled in Medicaid; it is unlikely to save lives; it is unaffordable in the long run; its current financing structure encourages fiscal irresponsibility; and it will eliminate more jobs than it creates.</AbstractText>
